Package: poissonCloud
Type: Package
Title: Poisson Models and a Digital Twin for Cloud Capacity Planning
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: person("Sharone Vanelle", "Ndomtchi", email = "sharonevanelle@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Starts from the Poisson distribution and shows where it breaks on
    real-looking web traffic (daily seasonality, bursts), then fixes it with a
    seasonal negative-binomial traffic model and a Hawkes self-exciting process.
    Includes a discrete-time digital twin of an autoscaling cluster (boot delay,
    queue, SLO), policy optimisation, anomaly detection, M/M/c queueing
    (Erlang C), a Shiny dashboard and a plumber API.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports: stats, graphics, utils, tools
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), knitr, rmarkdown, shiny, plumber, readxl
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
URL: https://github.com/sharone08/poissonCloud
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
